(7642622, 1241302, 52549, '<td valign="top">Another world, SO beautiful. Fantastic lighting. This beauty is going straight into my favourites.</td>', 'Another world, SO beautiful. Fantastic lighting. This beauty is going straight into my favourites.', '2019-09-30 04:10:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(7642640, 1241299, 114285, '<td valign="top">Wow you got totally ripped off!!!</td>', 'Wow you got totally ripped off!!!', '2019-09-30 07:42:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(7642642, 1241299, 135744, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Neat:</b></div><hr/><i> Wow you got totally ripped off!!! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>To be fair the quality isn''t great. I would love to have had the photo shoot on video. I had tried the previous night to take the same shot but was in a field too far to the left and didn''t have time to make it out to the road to get to the next field along. There was a small river between the fields.<br/> <br/>Anyway I came back on Saturday night having attempted to work out my position and this time shooting from the road to allow me to quickly move position. When I saw the glow I thought I was again too far to the left so dashed up the road with camera on tripod. Unfortunately there were some trees in the way so I ended up in a field. Anyway it all happened so quick and my quick release cable fell out which caused me major panic. I am not entirely sure why the photo looked so bad as the ISO was actually quite low. Prob me pressing the button on the camera or just the atmosphere or more likely a combination of factors. Anyway I will try again next month and hopefully improve (assuming a clear sky of course)</td>', 'Originally posted by Neat: Wow you got totally ripped off!!!   To be fair the quality isn''t great. I would love to have had the photo shoot on video. I had tried the previous night to take the same shot but was in a field too far to the left and didn''t have time to make it out to the road to get to the next field along. There was a small river between the fields. Anyway I came back on Saturday night having attempted to work out my position and this time shooting from the road to allow me to quickly move position. When I saw the glow I thought I was again too far to the left so dashed up the road with camera on tripod. Unfortunately there were some trees in the way so I ended up in a field. Anyway it all happened so quick and my quick release cable fell out which caused me major panic. I am not entirely sure why the photo looked so bad as the ISO was actually quite low. Prob me pressing the button on the camera or just the atmosphere or more likely a combination of factors. Anyway I will try again next month and hopefully improve (assuming a clear sky of course)', '2019-09-30 08:09:41.000000', NULL, 0),
